// NOT FROZEN. Draft, in the same sense as b04's: it exists so preflight has something
// concrete to test against, and freezing it is the user's act, at the same time as
// CRITERIA.md. A frozen criterion against an unfrozen config means nothing.
//
// Every field is b04's value verbatim except TWO -- tracked_coordinates and
// saddle_search_max_rise_eV -- so the two grids stay comparable and any difference in
// outcome is attributable to the chemistry rather than to a knob. Two more fields are
// listed below although they are UNCHANGED, because "we kept it" is a decision here and
// the reason is a measurement.
//
// tracked_coordinates -- SEVEN, not three, because this grid has two channels and both
//   must be readable off a trajectory by name. q_substitution = r(C-Cl) - r(C-O) and
//   q_elimination = r(C_beta-H) - r(O-H) are the two progress variables; their signs say
//   which channel a frame is on, and r(C-C) says whether an alkene is forming. Naming
//   them is not the same as expecting them: a trajectory that moves neither is a
//   perfectly good elastic result, and a trajectory that moves both is the information
//   this grid exists to collect.
//
// saddle_search_max_rise_eV = 10.0 -- the probe-phase, NON-BINDING value, not a
//   criterion. b04 measured what happens with 1.5: the ceiling refused the seed at step
//   0 (max_rise 1.5479) and the reaction's own saddle was invisible. Carrying 1.5 here
//   would be repeating a measurement whose answer is already known. The real ceiling is
//   an OUTPUT of the B block (DECISIONS_PENDING 4a) and this grid contributes to it.
//
// families -- stretch/compress/kick/bend, as b04. torsion is left OUT on purpose: the
//   only torsions here are the three methyl rotors, and they are symmetry rotors, so a
//   120 degree turn maps the structure onto a symmetry copy of itself. Ethanol measured
//   the cost of not knowing that -- 15 of 24 trials spent on a rotor that could not
//   reach anything (PRRS_STATUS.md 1.2). They stay reachable through the rotor
//   degradation path, which is where a methyl-rotation saddle would still show up.
//
// pair_cutoff_A = 4.0 -- UNCHANGED from b04. A draft of this grid raised it to 4.6 so
//   the base could sit further out. Measured on the corrected geometry, with the cutoff
//   as the ONLY variable: 152 candidates -> 24 selected at 4.0, and 191 -> 24 at 4.6.
//   Both are capped at max_directions, so the cutoff changes coverage (16% -> 13%) and
//   changes nothing about what gets selected. An earlier version of this comment said
//   raising it took gate 6 from PASS to FAIL; that conflated the cutoff change with the
//   methyl-polar-angle fix made in the same step, and the PASS belonged to the broken
//   geometry. Reach cannot be bought with the cutoff -- but neither is the cutoff what
//   lost it. See ../../docs/DECISIONS_PENDING.md, the direction-contract ruling.
// direction_mode = "sampled" —— 显式写出（用户裁决 2026-09-09）。探针期就是抽样，
//   因此这一格的每一条负结论在探针阶段一律 `unanswered`，不得读成"协同"。
//
//   **正式运行是否改 exhaustive，等首次探针给出成本后再决定，现在不预支。**
//   实测代价：源结构一处的完全枚举是 **504 个 coarse trial**（152 个方向 × 各自的幅度，
//   对 sampled 的 24 方向 / 86 trial），更深的微态还要加。而 16 原子的 s/trial 尚未测过 ——
//   b04 是 6 原子 39.5 s/trial，**不外推**。先用 sampled 量成本，再决定值不值这个价。

